  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through next Friday) \nIssued at 1050 PM CDT Thu Sep 17 2026\n\nConfidence is increasing for heat relief next week. The big ridge\nwill weaken and pull southwest as a trough develops over the \nUpper Midwest and Great Lakes. Models show this trough deepening\nand bringing lower heights across the TN Valley. NBM confidently\nlowers our high temperatures into the 80s by mid to late week.\nThese numbers are still warmer than normal, so no pumpkin spice \nweather just yet!\n\nThe breakdown of the strong ridge will allow chances for  \nscattered showers and storms to increase, but no substantial,\nprolonged rain is seen. The best chance for some rain will occur\nTuesday as the developing trough to our north drops a frontal \nzone into the area. Pops will top out at 30 to 50 percent most \nareas with 60 percent for the Plateau. Drier air is shown after \nTuesday.",
